Vita Moonlight Opus 1.6.1 CMake compatibility patch
Copyright (C) 2026 Vita Moonlight contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

Opus's CMake build adds the NEON implementation sources when NEON is presumed,
but it only defines the matching MAY_HAVE capability macros when runtime
detection is requested.  The public headers consequently omit declarations
used by those sources.  A Vita always exposes the same ARMv7 NEON capability,
so make the presumed configuration advertise the compiler capability too.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index a336daf..0879a17 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -590,6 +590,8 @@ if(NOT OPUS_DISABLE_INTRINSICS)
     if(OPUS_PRESUME_NEON)
       target_compile_definitions(opus
                                  PRIVATE
+                                 OPUS_ARM_MAY_HAVE_NEON
+                                 OPUS_ARM_MAY_HAVE_NEON_INTR
                                  OPUS_ARM_PRESUME_NEON
                                  OPUS_ARM_PRESUME_NEON_INTR)
     endif()
